From 99588a81a5c6171490dc22a4d56c46da3856a6f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DAKSH THAKUR <70480346+Just-DT21@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:21:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Restore the missing worker module so file processing
 works in production
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The deployed tree was missing spade/worker.py and spade/__init__.py, so the web
process started and reported a healthy /api/health while every upload died at
analysis time with "No module named spade.worker". Restore both files, add a
regression test that checks the module is on disk and runs real analysis and
optimisation jobs through the supervisor, and stop tracking the committed
__pycache__ artifacts now that a .gitignore keeps them and the private data
directories out of the repository.

