From 239f79d5f25bb16ac08ad80d103c8b96d522df45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DAKSH THAKUR <70480346+Just-DT21@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:21:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add a collapsible sidebar that remembers its state per
 browser
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The sidebar can now collapse to a 64px icon rail on desktop and become an
off-canvas drawer on narrow screens, so the main column keeps the freed width
instead of leaving label-shaped gaps. State lives in two classes on the app
shell, is persisted in localStorage with a safe expanded default when storage is
unavailable, and the toggle, menu button, Escape key and nav selection all keep
the accessibility attributes in step. Tests pin the element ids the JavaScript
depends on, the navigation set, and the class names shared with the stylesheet.

